{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-97635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a **clockwise** circular path with center $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $3\\text{ rad/s}.$ Given that the object is at the position $(2,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the position function of the particle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d4de5674ea680dd236f5b69d6a53d6a92c007bf6d9a46661b876ea41984f43e"} {"question" "q-97635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(2,0),$ we have that $r(0)=\\,2i,$ and we can conclude that the radius of the circle $R=2.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=2$ and $\\omega =-3\\text{ rad/s}$ (negative because the motion is clockwise), we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3t)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3t)\\,j) \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d4de5674ea680dd236f5b69d6a53d6a92c007bf6d9a46661b876ea41984f43e"} {"question" "q-97635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6bd