ile_sha256" "0d4de5674ea680dd236f5b69d6a53d6a92c007bf6d9a46661b876ea41984f43e"} {"question" "q-97631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(4,0),$ we have that $r(0)=4i,$ and we can conclude that the circle's radius is $R=4.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=4$ and $\\omega =1\\text{ rad/s},$ we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d4de5674ea680dd236f5b69d6a53d6a92c007bf6d9a46661b876ea41984f43e"} {"question" "q-97631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6bdca8b5d8aa64b959fc7306a04e3d1a5f55216bda2d412c0fa0b39360e67cc1"} {"question" "q-97631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d4de5674ea680dd236f5b69d6a53d6a92c007bf6d9a46661b876ea41984f43e"} {"question" "q-97631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r(t)=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)"] ["math" "r(t)=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\