fore, since we have $R=6$ and $\\omega =-\\pi \\text{ rad/s}$ (negative because the motion is clockwise), we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi t)\\,j) \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d4de5674ea680dd236f5b69d6a53d6a92c007bf6d9a46661b876ea41984f43e"} {"question" "q-97638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6bdca8b5d8aa64b959fc7306a04e3d1a5f55216bda2d412c0fa0b39360e67cc1"} {"question" "q-97638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d4de5674ea680dd236f5b69d6a53d6a92c007bf6d9a46661b876ea41984f43e"} {"question" "q-97638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r(t)=-6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j)"] ["math" "r(t)=6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j)"] ["math" "r(t)=6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j)"] ["math" "r(t)=\\pi (\\operatorname{cos}⁡6t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡6t\\,j)"] ["math" "r(t)=\\pi (\\operatorname{cos}⁡6t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡6t\\,j)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064391/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d4de5674ea680dd236f5b69d6a53d6a92c007bf6d9a46661b876ea41984f43e"} {"questio